<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0052/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0052/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0052/>;
    dc:modified '2008-11-11T15:25:45'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'water_evaporation_flux_from_canopy_where_land'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Unless indicated, a quantity is assumed to apply to the whole area of each horizontal grid box. The qualifier where_type specifies instead that the quantity applies only to the part of the grid box of the named type. \'Water\' means water in all phases. \'Canopy\' means the plant or vegetation canopy. Evaporation is the conversion of liquid or solid into vapor. (The conversion of solid alone into vapor is called \'sublimation\'.) In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \'flux\' implies per unit area, called \'flux density\' in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0052'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0054/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0054/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0054/>;
    dc:modified '2008-11-11T15:25:45'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'water_evaporation_flux_where_sea_ice'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Unless indicated, a quantity is assumed to apply to the whole area of each horizontal grid box. The qualifier where_type specifies instead that the quantity applies only to the part of the grid box of the named type. \'Water\' means water in all phases. Evaporation is the conversion of liquid or solid into vapor. (The conversion of solid alone into vapor is called \'sublimation\'.) In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \'flux\' implies per unit area, called \'flux density\' in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0054'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0223/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0223/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0223/>;
    dc:modified '2008-11-11T15:25:45'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'surface_snow_thickness_where_sea_ice'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The surface called \'surface\' means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. Unless indicated, a quantity is assumed to apply to the whole area of each horizontal grid box. The qualifier where_type specifies instead that the quantity applies only to the part of the grid box of the named type.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0223'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0227/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0227/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0227/>;
    dc:modified '2008-11-11T15:25:45'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'surface_temperature_where_land'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Unless indicated, a quantity is assumed to apply to the whole area of each horizontal grid box. The qualifier where_type specifies instead that the quantity applies only to the part of the grid box of the named type. The surface temperature is the (skin) temperature at the interface, not the bulk temperature of the medium above or below.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0227'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0228/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0228/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0228/>;
    dc:modified '2008-11-11T15:25:45'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'surface_temperature_where_open_sea'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The surface called \'surface\' means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. Unless indicated, a quantity is assumed to apply to the whole area of each horizontal grid box. The qualifier where_type specifies instead that the quantity applies only to the part of the grid box of the named type. The surface temperature is the (skin) temperature at the interface, not the bulk temperature of the medium above or below.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0228'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0229/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0229/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0229/>;
    dc:modified '2008-11-11T15:25:45'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'surface_temperature_where_snow'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The surface called \'surface\' means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. Unless indicated, a quantity is assumed to apply to the whole area of each horizontal grid box. The qualifier where_type specifies instead that the quantity applies only to the part of the grid box of the named type. The surface temperature is the (skin) temperature at the interface, not the bulk temperature of the medium above or below.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0229'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0233/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0233/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0233/>;
    dc:modified '2008-11-11T15:25:45'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'surface_upward_sensible_heat_flux_where_sea'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The surface called \'surface\' means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. Unless indicated, a quantity is assumed to apply to the whole area of each horizontal grid box. The qualifier where_type specifies instead that the quantity applies only to the part of the grid box of the named type. \'Upward\' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed upward (negative downward). The surface sensible heat flux, also called \'turbulent\' heat flux, is the exchange of heat between the surface and the air by motion of air. In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \'flux\' implies per unit area, called \'flux density\' in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0233'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0294/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0294/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0294/>;
    dc:modified '2008-11-11T15:25:45'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'surface_cover'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The surface called \'surface\' means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. A variable with the standard name of surface_cover contains strings which indicate the nature of the surface e.g. urban, forest, vegetation, land, sea_ice, open_sea. These strings have not yet been standardised. This standard name is a generalisation of land_cover.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0294'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0454/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0454/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0454/>;
    dc:modified '2008-11-11T15:25:45'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'precipitation_flux_onto_canopy_where_land'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Unless indicated, a quantity is assumed to apply to the whole area of each horizontal grid box. The qualifier where_type specifies instead that the quantity applies only to the part of the grid box of the named type. \'Canopy\' means the plant or vegetation canopy. In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \'flux\' implies per unit area, called \'flux density\' in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0454'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0575/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0575/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0575/>;
    dc:modified '2008-11-11T15:25:45'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'land_cover'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A variable with the standard name of land_cover contains strings which indicate the nature of the anthropogenic land use or vegetation e.g. urban, grass, needleleaf trees, ice. These strings have not yet been standardised. The alternative standard name of surface_cover is a generalisation of land_cover. Alternatively, the data variable may contain integers which can be translated to strings using flag_values and flag_meanings attributes.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0575'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0780/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0780/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0780/>;
    dc:modified '2008-11-11T15:25:45'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'surface_net_downward_radiative_flux_where_land'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The surface called "surface" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. "Downward" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed downward (negative upward). Net downward radiation is the difference between radiation from above (downwelling) and radiation from below (upwelling). Radiative flux is the sum of shortwave and longwave radiative fluxes. In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, "flux" implies per unit area, called "flux density" in physics. Unless indicated, a quantity is assumed to apply to the whole area of each horizontal grid box. The qualifier where_type specifies instead that the quantity applies only to the part of the grid box of the named type.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0780'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N23/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N23/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N23/>;
    dc:modified '2008-11-11T15:25:45'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'mole_fraction_of_chlorine dioxide_in_air'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Mole fraction is used in the construction mole_fraction_of_X_in_Y, where X is a material constituent of Y.  The chemical formula of chlorine dioxide is OClO.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV8N23'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N24/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N24/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N24/>;
    dc:modified '2008-11-11T15:25:45'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'mole_fraction_of_chlorine monoxide_in_air'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Mole fraction is used in the construction mole_fraction_of_X_in_Y, where X is a material constituent of Y.  The chemical formula of chlorine monoxide is ClO.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV8N24'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N26/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N26/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N26/>;
    dc:modified '2008-11-11T15:25:45'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'mole_fraction_of_dichlorine peroxide_in_air'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Mole fraction is used in the construction mole_fraction_of_X_in_Y, where X is a material constituent of Y.   The chemical formula of dichlorine peroxide is Cl2O2.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV8N26'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N38/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N38/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N38/>;
    dc:modified '2008-11-11T15:25:45'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'mole_fraction_of_hypochlorous acid_in_air'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Mole fraction is used in the construction mole_fraction_of_X_in_Y, where X is a material constituent of Y.  The chemical formula of hypochlorous acid is HOCl.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV8N38'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV11N1/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV11N1/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV11N1/>;
    dc:modified '2008-11-11T15:14:41'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'cloud_ice_mixing_ratio'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Cloud ice mixing ratio of a parcel of air is the ratio of the mass of ice to the mass of dry air.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV11N1'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV11N12/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV11N12/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV11N12/>;
    dc:modified '2008-11-11T15:14:41'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'minus_one_times_toa_outgoing_shortwave_flux'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Minus one times" means that the quantity described takes the opposite sign convention  to that for the quantity which has the same standard name apart from this phrase, i.e. the two quantities differ from one another by a factor of -1.  Shortwave means shortwave radiation. "toa" means top of atmosphere. The TOA outgoing shortwave flux is the reflected and scattered solar radiative flux i.e. the "upwelling" TOA shortwave flux, sometimes called the "outgoing shortwave radiation" or "OSR". In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, "flux" implies per unit area, called "flux density" in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV11N12'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV11N13/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV11N13/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV11N13/>;
    dc:modified '2008-11-11T15:14:41'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'toa_net_downward_longwave_flux_assuming_clear_sky'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A phrase assuming_condition indicates that the named quantity is the value which would obtain if all aspects of the system were unaltered except for the assumption of the circumstances specified by the condition. "longwave" means longwave radiation. "toa" means top of atmosphere. "Downward" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed downward (negative upward). Net downward radiation is the difference between radiation from above (downwelling) and radiation from below (upwelling). In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, "flux" implies per unit area, called "flux density" in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV11N13'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV11N4/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV11N4/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV11N4/>;
    dc:modified '2008-11-11T15:14:41'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'downward_heat_flux_in_floating_ice'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Downward" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed downward (negative upward). In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, "flux" implies per unit area, called "flux density" in physics.  "Floating ice" means any ice that is floating on water, e.g. on a sea or lake surface.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV11N4'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV11N5/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV11N5/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV11N5/>;
    dc:modified '2008-11-11T15:14:41'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'floating_ice_thickness'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Floating ice" means any ice that is floating on water, e.g. on a sea or lake surface.  "Thickness" means the vertical extent of the ice.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV11N5'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV11S2/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV11S2/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV11S2/>;
    dc:modified '2008-11-11T15:14:41'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'mole_fraction_of_chlorine_dioxide_in_air'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Mole fraction is used in the construction mole_fraction_of_X_in_Y, where X is a material constituent of Y. The chemical formula of chlorine dioxide is OClO.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV11S2'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV11S3/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV11S3/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV11S3/>;
    dc:modified '2008-11-11T15:14:41'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'mole_fraction_of_chlorine_monoxide_in_air'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Mole fraction is used in the construction mole_fraction_of_X_in_Y, where X is a material constituent of Y. The chemical formula of chlorine monoxide is ClO.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV11S3'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV11S5/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV11S5/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV11S5/>;
    dc:modified '2008-11-11T15:14:41'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'mole_fraction_of_hypochlorous_acid_in_air'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Mole fraction is used in the construction mole_fraction_of_X_in_Y, where X is a material constituent of Y. The chemical formula of hypochlorous acid is HOCl.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV11S5'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0034/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0034/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0034/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'water_volume_transport_into_ocean_from_rivers'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'Water\' means water in all phases. The water flux or volume transport into the ocean from rivers is the inflow to the ocean, often applied to the surface in ocean models.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0034'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0037/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0037/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0037/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'wind_mixing_energy_flux_into_ocean'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Wind is defined as a two-dimensional (horizontal) air velocity vector, with no vertical component. (Vertical motion in the atmosphere has the standard name upward_air_velocity.) In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \'flux\' implies per unit area, called \'flux density\' in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0037'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0056/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0056/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0056/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'water_flux_into_ocean'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'Water\' means water in all phases. The water flux into the ocean is the freshwater entering the sea water as a result of precipitation, evaporation, river inflow, sea ice effects and water flux correction (if applied). In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \'flux\' implies per unit area, called \'flux density\' in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0056'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0057/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0057/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0057/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'water_flux_into_ocean_from_rivers'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'Water\' means water in all phases. The water flux or volume transport into the ocean from rivers is the inflow to the ocean, often applied to the surface in ocean models. In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \'flux\' implies per unit area, called \'flux density\' in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0057'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N1/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N1/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N1/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'altimeter_range'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An altimeter operates by sending out a short pulse of radiation and measuring the time required for the pulse to return from the sea surface; this measurement is used to calculate the distance between the instrument and the sea surface.  That measurement is called the "altimeter range" and does not include any range corrections.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N1'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N10/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N10/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N10/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'depth_at_maximum_upward_derivative_of_sea_water_potential_temperature'@en ;
    skos:definition 'This quantity, often used to indicate the "thermocline depth", is the depth of the maximum vertical gradient of sea water potential temperature.  Depth is the vertical distance below the surface. Potential temperature is the temperature a parcel of air or sea water would have if moved adiabatically to sea level pressure.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N10'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N11/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N11/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N11/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'depth_of_isosurface_of_sea_water_potential_temperature'@en ;
    skos:definition 'This quantity, sometimes called the "isotherm depth", is the depth (if it exists) at which the sea water potential temperature equals some specified value. This value should be specified in a scalar coordinate variable. Depth is the vertical distance below the surface. Potential temperature is the temperature a parcel of air or sea water would have if moved adiabatically to sea level pressure.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N11'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N13/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N13/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N13/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'heat_flux_into_sea_water_due_to_newtonian_relaxation'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase.  The heat_flux_into_sea_water_due_to_newtonian_relaxation is  the heat flux resulting from the Newtonian relaxation of the sea surface temperature. In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, "flux" implies per unit area, called "flux density" in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N13'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N16/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N16/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N16/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'magnitude_of_derivative_of_position_wrt_model_level_number'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The quantity with standard name magnitude_of_derivative_of_position_wrt_model_level_number (known in differential geometry as a "scale factor") is | (dr/dk)ij|, where r(i,j,k) is the vector 3D position of the point with coordinate indices (i,j,k). It is a measure of the gridblock spacing in the z-direction.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N16'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N17/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N17/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N17/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'magnitude_of_derivative_of_position_wrt_x_coordinate_index'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The quantity with standard name magnitude_of_derivative_of_position_wrt_x_coordinate_index (known in differential geometry as a "scale factor") is | (dr/di)jk|, where r(i,j,k) is the vector 3D position of the point with coordinate indices (i,j,k). It is a measure of the gridblock spacing in the x-direction.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N17'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N18/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N18/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N18/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'magnitude_of_derivative_of_position_wrt_y_coordinate_index'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The quantity with standard name magnitude_of_derivative_of_position_wrt_y_coordinate_index (known in differential geometry as a "scale factor") is | (dr/dj)ik|, where r(i,j,k) is the vector 3D position of the point with coordinate indices (i,j,k). It is a measure of the gridblock spacing in the y-direction.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N18'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N2/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N2/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N2/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'altimeter_range_correction_due_to_dry_troposphere'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase.   To apply the altimeter range correction it must be added to the quantity with standard name altimeter_range.  "Correction_due_to_dry_troposphere" means a correction for dry gases in the troposphere, i.e. excluding the effect of liquid water.  Additional altimeter range corrections are given by the quantities with standard names altimeter_range_correction_due_to_wet_troposphere, altimeter_range_correction_due_to_ionosphere, sea_surface_height_correction_due_to_air_pressure_at_low_frequency and sea_surface_height_correction_due_to_air_pressure_and_wind_at_high_frequency.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N2'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N21/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N21/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N21/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'model_level_number_at_sea_floor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The quantity with standard name model_level_number_at_sea_floor is the depth of the ocean expressed in model levels. This could be a non-integer value because some ocean models use partial cells close to the sea floor.  For example, if this field were 23.4 at some location, it would mean the water column at that point comprised 23 full model levels plus 40% occupancy of the lowest (24th) gridcell.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N21'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N23/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N23/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N23/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'ocean_rigid_lid_pressure'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Ocean rigid lid pressure" means the pressure at the surface of an ocean model assuming that it is bounded above by a rigid lid.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N23'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N25/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N25/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N25/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'ocean_vertical_diffusivity'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Vertical diffusivity" means the vertical component of diffusivity due to motion which is not resolved on the grid scale of the model.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N25'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N26/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N26/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N26/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'ocean_vertical_heat_diffusivity'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Vertical heat diffusivity" means the vertical component of the diffusivity of heat due to motion which is not resolved on the grid scale of the model.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N26'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N27/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N27/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N27/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'ocean_vertical_momentum_diffusivity'@en ;
    skos:definition 'ocean_vertical_momentum_diffusivity'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N27'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N29/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N29/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N29/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'ocean_vertical_salt_diffusivity'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Vertical salt diffusivity" means the vertical component of the diffusivity of salt due to motion which is not resolved on the grid scale of the model.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N29'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N3/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N3/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N3/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'altimeter_range_correction_due_to_ionosphere'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase.   To apply the altimeter range correction it must be added to the quantity with standard name altimeter_range.  "Correction_due_to_ionosphere" means a correction for the atmosphere\'s electron content in the ionosphere. Additional altimeter range corrections are given by the quantities with standard names altimeter_range_correction_due_to_wet_troposphere, altimeter_range_correction_due_to_dry_troposphere, sea_surface_height_correction_due_to_air_pressure_at_low_frequency and sea_surface_height_correction_due_to_air_pressure_and_wind_at_high_frequency.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N3'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N30/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N30/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N30/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'ocean_vertical_tracer_diffusivity'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Vertical tracer diffusivity" means the vertical component of the diffusivity of tracers, i.e. heat and salinity, due to motion which is not resolved on the grid scale of the model.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N30'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N31/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N31/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N31/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'ocean_vertical_tracer_diffusivity_due_to_convection'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. "Vertical tracer diffusivity" means the vertical component of the diffusivity of tracers, i.e. heat and salinity, due to motion which is not resolved on the grid scale of the model.  Convective mixing in the ocean is sometimes modelled as an enhanced diffusivity.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N31'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N32/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N32/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N32/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'ocean_vertical_tracer_diffusivity_due_to_wind_mixing'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. "Vertical tracer diffusivity" means the vertical component of the diffusivity of tracers, i.e. heat and salinity, due to motion which is not resolved on the grid scale of the model.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N32'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N33/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N33/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N33/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'richardson_number_in_sea_water'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Richardson number is a measure of dynamic stability and can be used to diagnose the existence of turbulent flow.  It is defined as the ratio of the buoyant suppression of turbulence (i.e. how statically stable or unstable the conditions are)  to the kinetic energy available to generate turbulence  in a shear flow.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N33'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N35/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N35/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N35/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sea_surface_height_amplitude_due_to_earth_tide'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. Tides are a significant contributor to the observed sea surface height; earth tide means the solid earth tide.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N35'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N36/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N36/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N36/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sea_surface_height_amplitude_due_to_equilibrium_ocean_tide'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. Tides are a significant contributor to the observed sea surface height; equilibrium ocean tide refers to the long period ocean tide.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N36'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N37/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N37/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N37/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sea_surface_height_amplitude_due_to_geocentric_ocean_tide'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. Tides are a significant contributor to the observed sea surface height; geocentric ocean tide means the sum total of ocean tide and load tide.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N37'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N38/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N38/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N38/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sea_surface_height_amplitude_due_to_non_equilibrium_ocean_tide'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. Tides are a significant contributor to the observed sea surface height; non equilibrium ocean tide refers to the long period ocean tide.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N38'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N39/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N39/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N39/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sea_surface_height_amplitude_due_to_pole_tide'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. Tides are a significant contributor to the observed sea surface height; the pole tide occurs due to variations in the earth\'s rotation.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N39'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N4/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N4/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N4/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'altimeter_range_correction_due_to_wet_troposphere'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase.   To apply the altimeter range correction it must be added to the quantity with standard name altimeter_range.  "Correction_due_to_wet_troposphere" means a correction for the effect of liquid water in the troposphere.  Additional altimeter range corrections are given by the quantities with standard names altimeter_range_correction_due_to_dry_troposphere, altimeter_range_correction_due_to_ionosphere, sea_surface_height_correction_due_to_air_pressure_at_low_frequency and sea_surface_height_correction_due_to_air_pressure_and_wind_at_high_frequency.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N4'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N41/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N41/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N41/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sea_surface_height_correction_due_to_air_pressure_and_wind_at_high_frequency'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. "Air pressure and wind at high frequency" means variations in air pressure with periods shorter  than 20 days. These give rise to corresponding variations in sea surface topography. The quantity sea_surface_height_correction_due_to_air_pressure_and_wind_at_high_frequency  should be applied by adding it to the quantity with standard name altimeter_range.  Additional altimeter range corrections are given by the quantities with standard names altimeter_range_correction_due_to_wet_troposphere, altimeter_range_correction_due_to_dry_troposphere, altimeter_range_correction_due_to_ionosphere and sea_surface_height_correction_due_to_air_pressure_at_low_frequency.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N41'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N42/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N42/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N42/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sea_surface_height_correction_due_to_air_pressure_at_low_frequency'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. "Air pressure at low frequency" means variations in air pressure with periods longer than 20 days. These give rise to corresponding variations in sea surface topography. The quantity sea_surface_height_correction_due_to_air_pressure_at_low_frequency is commonly called the "inverted barometer effect" and the correction should be applied by adding it to the quantity with standard name altimeter_range.  Additional altimeter range corrections are given by the quantities with standard names altimeter_range_correction_due_to_wet_troposphere, altimeter_range_correction_due_to_dry_troposphere, altimeter_range_correction_due_to_ionosphere and sea_surface_height_correction_due_to_air_pressure_and_wind_at_high_frequency.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N42'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N43/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N43/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N43/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'surface_backwards_scattering_coefficient_of_radar_wave'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The scattering/absorption/attenuation coefficient is assumed to be an integral over all wavelengths, unless a coordinate of radiation_wavelength is included to specify the wavelength. Scattering of radiation is its deflection from its incident path without loss of energy. Backwards scattering refers to the sum of scattering into all backward angles i.e. scattering_angle exceeding pi/2 radians. A scattering_angle should not be specified with this quantity.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N43'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N44/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N44/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N44/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'tendency_of_potential_energy_content_of_ocean_layer_due_to_convection'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. "tendency_of_X" means derivative of X with respect to time. "Content" indicates a quantity per unit area. "Layer" means any layer with upper and lower boundaries that have constant values in some vertical coordinate. There must be a vertical coordinate variable indicating the extent of the layer(s). If the layers are model layers, the vertical coordinate can be model_level_number, but it is recommended to specify a physical coordinate (in a scalar or auxiliary coordinate variable) as well. Potential energy is the sum of the gravitational potential energy relative to the geoid and the centripetal potential energy. (The geopotential is the specific potential energy.)'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N44'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N45/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N45/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N45/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'tendency_of_potential_energy_content_of_ocean_layer_due_to_diffusion'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. "tendency_of_X" means derivative of X with respect to time. "Content" indicates a quantity per unit area. "Layer" means any layer with upper and lower boundaries that have constant values in some vertical coordinate. There must be a vertical coordinate variable indicating the extent of the layer(s). If the layers are model layers, the vertical coordinate can be model_level_number, but it is recommended to specify a physical coordinate (in a scalar or auxiliary coordinate variable) as well. Potential energy is the sum of the gravitational potential energy relative to the geoid and the centripetal potential energy. (The geopotential is the specific potential energy.)'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N45'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N46/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N46/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N46/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'vertical_component_of_ocean_xy_tracer_diffusivity'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The vertical_component_of_ocean_xy_tracer_diffusivity means the vertical component of the diffusivity of tracers in the ocean due to lateral mixing. This quantity could appear in formulations of lateral diffusivity in which "lateral" does not mean "iso-level", e.g. it would not be used for isopycnal diffusivity. "Tracer diffusivity" means the diffusivity of heat and salinity due to motion which is not resolved on the grid scale of the model.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N46'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N47/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N47/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N47/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'virtual_salt_flux_into_sea_water'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The virtual_salt_flux_into_sea_water is the salt flux that would have the same effect on the sea surface salinity as the water_flux_out_of_sea_water. It includes the effects of precipitation, evaporation, river outflow, sea-ice and any water flux relaxation(s) and correction(s) that may have been applied. In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, "flux" implies per unit area, called "flux density" in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N47'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N48/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N48/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N48/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'virtual_salt_flux_into_sea_water_due_to_newtonian_relaxation'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. The virtual_salt_flux_into_sea_water_due_to_newtonian_relaxation is the salt flux that would have the same effect on the sea surface salinity as water_flux_out_of_sea_water_due_to_newtonian_relaxation. In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, "flux" implies per unit area, called "flux density" in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N48'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N49/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N49/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N49/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'water_flux_into_sea_water_without_flux_correction'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Water means water in all phases. The water_flux_into_sea_water_without_flux_correction  is the freshwater entering as a result of precipitation, evaporation, river inflow and sea ice effects.  The total water flux including any flux relaxation(s) or correction(s) is described by the standard name water_flux_into_sea_water.  In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, "flux" implies per unit area, called "flux density" in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N49'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N5/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N5/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N5/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'angle_of_rotation_from_east_to_x'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The quantity with standard name angle_of_rotation_from_east_to_x is the angle, anticlockwise reckoned positive, between due East and (dr/di)jk, where r(i,j,k) is the vector 3D position of the point with coordinate indices (i,j,k).  It could be used for rotating vector fields between model space and latitude-longitude space.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N5'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N51/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N51/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N51/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'water_flux_out_of_sea_water'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The quantity water_flux_out_of_sea_water is the quantity with  standard name water_flux_into_sea_water multiplied by -1. "Water" means water in all phases. The water flux out of sea water is the freshwater leaving as a result of precipitation, evaporation, river outflow, sea-ice and any water flux relaxation(s) and correction(s) that may have been applied. In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, "flux" implies per unit area, called "flux density" in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N51'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N52/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N52/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N52/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'water_flux_out_of_sea_water_due_to_newtonian_relaxation'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. The water_flux_out_of_sea_water_due_to_newtonian_relaxation is the freshwater leaving as a result of the Newtonian relaxation of the sea surface salinity. In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, "flux" implies per unit area, called "flux density" in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N52'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N6/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N6/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N6/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'angle_of_rotation_from_east_to_y'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The quantity with standard name angle_of_rotation_from_east_to_y is the angle, anticlockwise reckoned positive, between due East and (dr/dj)ik, where r(i,j,k) is the vector 3D position of the point with coordinate indices (i,j,k).  It could be used for rotating vector fields between model space and latitude-longitude space.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N6'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N9/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N9/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N9/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'cell_area'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Cell_area" is the horizontal area of a gridcell.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10N9'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10S1/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10S1/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10S1/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'water_flux_into_sea_water'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Water" means water in all phases. The water flux into sea water is the freshwater entering as a result of precipitation, evaporation, river inflow, sea ice effects and water flux relaxation and correction (if applied). In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, "flux" implies per unit area, called "flux density" in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10S1'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10S4/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10S4/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10S4/>;
    dc:modified '2008-10-21T10:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'wind_mixing_energy_flux_into_sea_water'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Wind is defined as a two-dimensional (horizontal) air velocity vector, with no vertical component. (Vertical motion in the atmosphere has the standard name upward_air_velocity.) In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, "flux" implies per unit area, called "flux density" in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV10S4'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N133/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N133/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N133/>;
    dc:modified '2008-06-10T23:59:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'upward_eliassen_palm_flux'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Eliassen Palm flux" is a widely used vector in the meridional plane, and the divergence of this flux appears as a forcing in the Transformed Eulerian mean formulation of the zonal mean zonal wind equation.  "Upward" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed upward (negative downward).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV8N133'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N134/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N134/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N134/>;
    dc:modified '2008-06-10T23:59:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'upward_flux_of_eastward_momentum_due_to_nonorographic_eastward_gravity_waves'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase.  Upward indicates a vector component which is positive when directed upward (negative downward).  Momentum flux is dimensionally equivalent to stress and pressure. It is a tensor quantity. In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, "flux" implies per unit area, called "flux density" in physics.  The total upward momentum flux due to gravity waves is the sum of the fluxes due to orographic gravity waves and nonorographic waves.  The upward momentum flux due to orographic gravity waves has the standard name upward_flux_of_eastward_momentum_due_to_orographic_gravity_waves.  The total upward momentum flux due to nonorographic gravity waves is the sum of the fluxes due to eastward and westward propagating waves.  The latter has the standard name upward_flux_of_eastward_momentum_due_to_nonorographic_westward _gravity_waves.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV8N134'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N135/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N135/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N135/>;
    dc:modified '2008-06-10T23:59:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'upward_flux_of_eastward_momentum_due_to_nonorographic_westward_gravity_waves'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase.  Upward indicates a vector component which is positive when directed upward (negative downward).  Momentum flux is dimensionally equivalent to stress and pressure. It is a tensor quantity. In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, "flux" implies per unit area, called "flux density" in physics.  The total upward momentum flux due to gravity waves is the sum of the fluxes due to orographic gravity waves and nonorographic waves.  The upward momentum flux due to orographic gravity waves has the standard name upward_flux_of_eastward_momentum_due_to_orographic_gravity_waves.  The total upward momentum flux due to nonorographic gravity waves is the sum of the fluxes due to eastward and westward propagating waves.  The former has the standard name upward_flux_of_eastward_momentum_due_to_nonorographic_eastward _gravity_waves.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV8N135'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N136/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N136/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N136/>;
    dc:modified '2008-06-10T23:59:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'upward_flux_of_eastward_momentum_due_to_orographic_gravity_waves'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase.  Upward indicates a vector component which is positive when directed upward (negative downward).  Momentum flux is dimensionally equivalent to stress and pressure. It is a tensor quantity. In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, "flux" implies per unit area, called "flux density" in physics.  The total upward momentum flux due to gravity waves is the sum of the fluxes due to orographic gravity waves and nonorographic waves.  The total upward momentum flux due to nonorographic gravity waves is the sum of the fluxes due to eastward and westward propagating waves.  These quantities have the standard names upward_flux_of_eastward_momentum_due_to_nonorographic_eastward _gravity_waves and upward_flux_of_eastward_momentum_due_to_nonorographic_westward _gravity_waves, respectively.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV8N136'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N41/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N41/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N41/>;
    dc:modified '2008-06-10T23:59:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'mole_fraction_of_methyl_chloride_in_air'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Mole fraction is used in the construction mole_fraction_of_X_in_Y, where X is a material constituent of Y.  The chemical formula of methyl chloride is CH3Cl.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV8N41'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N67/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N67/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N67/>;
    dc:modified '2008-06-10T23:59:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'northward_eliassen_palm_flux'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Eliassen Palm flux" is a widely used vector in the meridional plane, and the divergence of this flux appears as a forcing in the Transformed Eulerian mean formulation of the zonal mean zonal wind equation.  "Northward" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed northward (negative southward).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV8N67'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N68/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N68/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N68/>;
    dc:modified '2008-06-10T23:59:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'northward_heat_flux_due_to_eddy_advection'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. "Northward" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed northward (negative southward).  In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, "flux" implies per unit area, called "flux density" in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV8N68'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N69/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N69/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N69/>;
    dc:modified '2008-06-10T23:59:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'northward_transformed_eulerian_mean_velocity'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Northward" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed northward (negative southward).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV8N69'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N9/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N9/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N9/>;
    dc:modified '2008-06-10T23:59:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'eastward_transformed_eulerian_mean_velocity'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Eastward indicates a vector component which is positive when directed eastward (negative westward).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV8N9'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV9S2/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV9S2/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV9S2/>;
    dc:modified '2008-06-10T23:59:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'northward_eliassen_palm_flux_in_air'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Eliassen Palm flux" is a widely used vector in the meridional plane, and the divergence of this flux appears as a forcing in the Transformed Eulerian mean formulation of the zonal mean zonal wind equation. "Northward" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed northward (negative southward).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV9S2'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV9S3/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV9S3/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV9S3/>;
    dc:modified '2008-06-10T23:59:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'northward_heat_flux_in_air_due_to_eddy_advection'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. "Northward" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed northward (negative southward). In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, "flux" implies per unit area, called "flux density" in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV9S3'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV9S5/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV9S5/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV9S5/>;
    dc:modified '2008-06-10T23:59:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'upward_eastward_momentum_flux_in_air_due_to_nonorographic_eastward_gravity_waves'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. "Upward" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed upward (negative downward). "Eastward" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed eastward (negative westward). "Upward eastward" indicates the ZX component of a tensor. An upward eastward momentum flux is an upward flux of eastward momentum, which accelerates the upper medium eastward and the lower medium westward.  Momentum flux is dimensionally equivalent to stress and pressure.  In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, "flux" implies per unit area, called "flux density" in physics. The total upward eastward momentum flux due to gravity waves is the sum of the fluxes due to orographic gravity waves and nonorographic waves. The upward eastward momentum flux due to orographic gravity waves has the standard name upward_eastward_momentum_flux_in_air_due_to_orographic_gravity_waves. The total upward eastward momentum flux due to nonorographic gravity waves is the sum of the fluxes due to eastward and westward propagating waves. The latter has the standard name upward_eastward_momentum_flux_in_air_due_to_nonorographic_westward_gravity_waves.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV9S5'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV9S6/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV9S6/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV9S6/>;
    dc:modified '2008-06-10T23:59:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'upward_eastward_momentum_flux_in_air_due_to_nonorographic_westward_gravity_waves'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. "Upward" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed upward (negative downward).  "Eastward" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed eastward (negative westward).  "Upward eastward" indicates the ZX component of a tensor. An upward eastward momentum flux is an upward flux of eastward momentum, which accelerates the upper medium eastward and the lower medium westward.  Momentum flux is dimensionally equivalent to stress and pressure.  In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, "flux" implies per unit area, called "flux density" in physics. The total upward eastward momentum flux due to gravity waves is the sum of the fluxes due to orographic gravity waves and nonorographic waves. The upward eastward momentum flux due to orographic gravity waves has the standard name upward_eastward_momentum_flux_in_air_due_to_orographic_gravity_waves. The total upward eastward momentum flux due to nonorographic gravity waves is the sum of the fluxes due to eastward and westward propagating waves. The former has the standard name upward_eastward_momentum_flux_in_air_due_to_nonorographic_eastward _gravity_waves.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV9S6'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV9S7/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV9S7/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV9S7/>;
    dc:modified '2008-06-10T23:59:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'upward_eastward_momentum_flux_in_air_due_to_orographic_gravity_waves'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. "Upward" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed upward (negative downward).  "Eastward" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed eastward (negative westward).  "Upward eastward" indicates the ZX component of a tensor. An upward eastward momentum flux is an upward flux of eastward momentum, which accelerates the upper medium eastward and the lower medium westward.  Momentum flux is dimensionally equivalent to stress and pressure.  In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, "flux" implies per unit area, called "flux density" in physics. The total upward eastward momentum flux due to gravity waves is the sum of the fluxes due to orographic gravity waves and nonorographic waves. The total upward eastward momentum flux due to nonorographic gravity waves is the sum of the fluxes due to eastward and westward propagating waves. These quantities have the standard names upward_eastward_momentum_flux_in_air_due_to_nonorographic_eastward_gravity_waves and upward_eastward_momentum_flux_in_air_due_to_nonorographic_westward_gravity_waves, respectively.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV9S7'^^xsd:string .
