<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N78/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N78/>;
    dc:modified '2008-04-15T14:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sea_surface_wind_wave_mean_period_from_variance_spectral_density_second_frequency_moment'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The wind wave directional spectrum can be written as a  five dimensional function S(t,x,y,f,theta) where t is time, x and y are horizontal coordinates (such as longitude and latitude), f is frequency and theta is direction.  S can be integrated over direction, thus S1= integral(S dtheta).  Frequency moments, M(n) of S1 can then be calculated as follows: M(n) = integral(S1 f^n df), where f^n is f to the power of n.  The second wave period, T(m2), is calculated as the square root of the ratio M(0)/M(2).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV8N78'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N79/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N79/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N79/>;
    dc:modified '2008-04-15T14:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'specific_kinetic_energy_of_sea_water'@en ;
    skos:definition '"specific" means per unit mass.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV8N79'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N82/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N82/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N82/>;
    dc:modified '2008-04-15T14:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'surface_upward_water_vapor_flux_in_air'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The surface called "surface" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere.  "Upward" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed upward (negative downward).  In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, "flux" implies per unit area, called "flux density" in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV8N82'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N83/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N83/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N83/>;
    dc:modified '2008-04-15T14:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'tendency_of_eastward_wind_due_to_eliassen_palm_flux_divergence'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. "Eastward" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed eastward (negative westward).  "Eliassen Palm flux" is a widely used vector in the meridional plane, and the divergence of this flux appears as a forcing in the Transformed Eulerian mean formulation of the zonal mean zonal wind equation.  Thus, "eastward_wind" here will generally be the zonally averaged eastward wind.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV8N83'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N84/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N84/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N84/>;
    dc:modified '2008-04-15T14:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'tendency_of_eastward_wind_due_to_nonorographic_gravity_wave_drag'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. "Eastward" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed eastward (negative westward).  The total tendency of the eastward wind due to gravity waves has the standard name tendency_of_eastward_wind_due_to_gravity_wave_drag.  It is the sum of the tendencies due to orographic gravity waves and nonorographic waves.  The tendency of eastward wind due to orographic gravity waves has the standard name tendency_of_eastward_wind_due_to_orographic_gravity_wave_drag.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV8N84'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N85/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N85/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N85/>;
    dc:modified '2008-04-15T14:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'tendency_of_eastward_wind_due_to_numerical_artefacts'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. "Eastward" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed eastward (negative westward).  The total tendency of the eastward wind will include a variety of numerical and diffusive effects: a variable with this standard name is sometimes needed to allow the momentum budget to be closed.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV8N85'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N86/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N86/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8N86/>;
    dc:modified '2008-04-15T14:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'tendency_of_eastward_wind_due_to_orographic_gravity_wave_drag'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. "Eastward" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed eastward (negative westward).  The total tendency of the eastward wind due to gravity waves has the standard name tendency_of_eastward_wind_due_to_gravity_wave_drag.  It is the sum of the tendencies due to orographic gravity waves and nonorographic waves.  The tendency of eastward wind due to nonorographic gravity waves has the standard name tendency_of_eastward_wind_due_to_nonorographic_gravity_wave_drag.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV8N86'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8NS1/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8NS1/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV8NS1/>;
    dc:modified '2008-04-15T14:00:00'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'mass_fraction_of_convective_cloud_condensed_water_in_air'@en ;
    skos:definition '"condensed_water" means liquid and ice. Mass fraction is used in the construction mass_fraction_of_X_in_Y, where X is a material constituent of Y. It means the ratio of the mass of X to the mass of Y (including X).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFV8NS1'^^xsd:string .
